+// applies to every StandardPBR material's own roughnessFactor param --
+// see overrideFloatMaterialParamIfPresent()'s own header comment for why
+// this is a plain boolean flag with ONE hardcoded value, not a
+// user-supplied number: this tool needs exactly one canonical, always-
+// wrong render to prove the gate discriminates, not a general fuzzing
+// knob, and a fixed constant sidesteps any "0.0 the sentinel for no
+// perturbation" vs. "0.0 a legitimate override value" ambiguity a
+// float CLI argument would otherwise carry.
+constexpr float kPerturbedRoughnessValue = 0.02F;
